  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 233 PM MST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nUpper level system is on tract, with a closed low dropping south\nalong the Lower Colorado River Valley, and increasing moisture and\ndiffluence aloft. \n\nA few thunderstorms over Cochise County, AZ will likely work into\nparts of Hidalgo County, NM in the next hour or two. Otherwise,\nexpect showers to become light to moderate as they increase in\ncoverage across the area, especially after dark.\n\nNBM/ForeastBuilder tried to produce a bit too much rain/snow mix\nover the Sacramento Mountains. Expect nearly-saturated conditions\nand a cold rain late tonight into Saturday, with accumulating snow\nlevels above 10-11K feet, and brief mixing down to around 9000 \nfeet, with no impacts. Most areas will see beneficial rainfall\namounts of around 0.10 to 0.25 inches from this system, and a few\npockets over 0.50 inches, mainly east of El Paso.\n\nTomorrow will be soup or stew weather over ELP and LRU. Cloudy, \nshowery, and damp, with highs stuck in the upper-50s in the\nlowlands, and upper-30s in the Sacramentos. \n\nQuieter weather overall next week, though a disorganized trough\nwill skirt the area Tuesday night, with a spotty shower or two not\nout of the question. Otherwise, expect slowly warming\ntemperatures, back to near normal (lower-70s in the lowlands) by\nWednesday.",
